01:31:57,700 --> 01:31:59,520
Cause I'm running really low on wheat.

1420
01:32:03,280 --> 01:32:04,040
Thank you.

1421
01:32:05,820 --> 01:32:06,920
They can make more.

1422
01:32:07,160 --> 01:32:08,020
They have a farm.

1423
01:32:13,140 --> 01:32:14,120
I'll take some apples.

1424
01:32:14,580 --> 01:32:15,180
Why not?

1425
01:32:21,530 --> 01:32:22,570
Cause apparently...

1426
01:32:24,210 --> 01:32:24,610
Honeydapple!

1427
01:32:25,870 --> 01:32:26,970
Wonder how good that is.

1428
01:32:28,450 --> 01:32:29,330
Maybe it's like...

1429
01:32:29,330 --> 01:32:29,950
Just as good as meat.

1430
01:32:37,370 --> 01:32:38,350
See that door is open.

1431
01:32:38,450 --> 01:32:39,590
That means I probably was here.

1432
01:32:43,180 --> 01:32:44,160
Yeah, I think I was here.

1433
01:32:48,710 --> 01:32:50,070
This song is on repeat.

1434
01:33:06,720 --> 01:33:07,940
Not seeing a swamp.

1435
01:33:11,250 --> 01:33:13,950
Sometimes I find the green guys in the caverns, too.

1436
01:33:14,090 --> 01:33:14,830
But it's kind of rare.

1437
01:33:22,500 --> 01:33:22,860
Weeeeaw.

1438
01:33:40,040 --> 01:33:42,440
There's definitely a way to create the green goo.

1439
01:33:44,120 --> 01:33:44,960
In a factory.

1440
01:33:45,400 --> 01:33:46,300
Like there has to be.

1441
01:33:57,410 --> 01:33:58,890
Elytra would help so much right now.

1442
01:34:09,120 --> 01:34:09,600
But she?

1443
01:34:09,740 --> 01:34:10,040
Definitely.

1444
01:34:11,640 --> 01:34:12,580
For a second I was like, wait...

1445
01:34:12,580 --> 01:34:13,640
Is there horse meat in this game?

1446
01:34:15,100 --> 01:34:16,240
I don't think there is.

1447
01:34:16,400 --> 01:34:17,640
Which is kind of weird when you think about it.

1448
01:34:17,640 --> 01:34:17,980
Why not?

1449
01:34:19,680 --> 01:34:20,960
Why isn't there horse meat?

1450
01:34:22,120 --> 01:34:23,260
I wanna eat horses.

1451
01:34:44,290 --> 01:34:46,170
I predict swamp on the other side of this mountain.

1452
01:34:46,690 --> 01:34:47,350
Or hill.

1453
01:34:52,180 --> 01:34:55,620
Based on my calculations, we should be... that's a jungle.

1454
01:34:57,440 --> 01:34:58,340
Kinda close?

1455
01:35:01,300 --> 01:35:02,320
Eh, maybe not.

1456
01:35:11,780 --> 01:35:14,120
You can totally feel the difference, by the way, with this meat.

1457
01:35:14,340 --> 01:35:15,560
Like, I've been sprinting for ages.

1458
01:35:16,480 --> 01:35:17,400
With no issue.

1459
01:35:21,400 --> 01:35:25,220
True pain would be playing Minecraft, and only having, uh, berries to heal with.

1460
01:35:30,410 --> 01:35:32,610
I think that would- I think that could drive anyone mad.

1461
01:35:32,750 --> 01:35:34,870
You know, it's- it's almost worse than waterboarding.

1462
01:35:36,110 --> 01:35:38,930
Just put someone in a room with Minecraft, and tell them to survive.

1463
01:35:40,610 --> 01:35:41,430
With only that.

1464
01:35:43,270 --> 01:35:44,470
Alright, grab this.

1465
01:35:52,320 --> 01:35:53,320
Shit's on fire, yo.

1466
01:36:03,340 --> 01:36:05,460
I forgot why I needed paper, but I needed it.

1467
01:36:17,790 --> 01:36:19,010
I just wanna see something here.

1468
01:36:27,050 --> 01:36:31,710
Place a train- oh, so it's actually- it does reveal more in that scenario there.

1469
01:36:32,850 --> 01:36:36,130
Use a mechanical press and basin to create fewer items or more.

1470
01:36:36,170 --> 01:36:37,890
I feel like I've done that, like, a lot.

1471
01:36:47,760 --> 01:36:51,420
There's also, uh, achievements for the other part of create.

1472
01:36:53,180 --> 01:36:55,480
Not really delved too deep into that yet.

1473
01:37:02,560 --> 01:37:08,120
Man, trains must be, like, the end game of create, you know, with all the stuff you need to make them.

1474
01:37:10,860 --> 01:37:12,740
It has been hell to get to this place.

1475
01:37:13,080 --> 01:37:14,220
But a good kind of hell, you know?

1476
01:37:14,780 --> 01:37:16,560
But man, you gotta go through a lot of hoops.

1477
01:37:18,200 --> 01:37:19,240
To reach this part.

1478
01:37:23,900 --> 01:37:26,720
And I'm talking like a proper, uh, connected railroad.

1479
01:37:32,280 --> 01:37:33,640
Dude, where is this swamp?

1480
01:37:37,190 --> 01:37:38,890
Have I not just been going east?

1481
01:37:39,190 --> 01:37:41,530
Like, we should be near spawn.

1482
01:37:54,740 --> 01:37:55,200
Oh!

1483
01:37:57,080 --> 01:37:58,620
That lo- wait, that's acacia.

1484
01:37:58,700 --> 01:37:59,360
That's not swamp.

1485
01:38:00,780 --> 01:38:02,100
That's, uh, well, acacia.

1486
01:38:02,300 --> 01:38:03,140
Acacia biome.

1487
01:38:04,480 --> 01:38:05,800
Not sure what you would call that.

1488
01:38:11,990 --> 01:38:14,150
But maybe it's an indicator of something.

1489
01:38:26,320 --> 01:38:27,600
Look at all this meat I'm gathering.

1490
01:38:42,450 --> 01:38:43,410
I need a buggy.

1491
01:38:43,890 --> 01:38:45,290
Something that drives off-road.

1492
01:38:54,580 --> 01:38:55,660
What even is that?

1493
01:38:55,780 --> 01:38:57,080
Like, how is this allowed to happen?

1494
01:38:58,860 --> 01:39:03,020
Couldn't you make a simple, if block not surrounded by anything in air, don't make?

1495
01:39:06,330 --> 01:39:08,590
Definitely more complicated than that, probably, but still.

1496
01:39:22,180 --> 01:39:23,980
Right on the other side of this hill is the swamp.

1497
01:39:24,260 --> 01:39:24,940
I remember.

1498
01:39:34,100 --> 01:39:35,000
Sorry, guys.

1499
01:39:35,380 --> 01:39:37,120
I need you to- I need you to die.

1500
01:39:45,700 --> 01:39:47,200
Okay, I'm actually lost then.

1501
01:39:49,620 --> 01:39:50,680
There's villages here.

1502
01:39:57,210 --> 01:39:59,310
Oh, I'm going so far from home, man.

1503
01:40:01,270 --> 01:40:04,670
How on earth are you supposed to farm this shit to make glue?

1504
01:40:08,580 --> 01:40:13,220
This is like the craziest, uh, bottleneck of all time.

1505
01:40:27,350 --> 01:40:29,970
Dude, I feel like I've overshot.

1506
01:40:31,750 --> 01:40:32,470
By miles.

1507
01:40:32,770 --> 01:40:35,590
Because usually it doesn't take this long to get home when I'm at spawn, you know?

1508
01:40:42,460 --> 01:40:45,140
I don't know how I did this, but I fucked it up for sure.

1509
01:40:48,880 --> 01:40:50,260
I'm gonna go a little north now.

1510
01:40:58,010 --> 01:40:58,950
I'll take some of these.

1511
01:41:03,350 --> 01:41:04,970
My budding jalapeno business.

1512
01:41:19,120 --> 01:41:21,360
Dude, if I see a portal, I'm actually just gonna go to the nether.

1513
01:41:25,920 --> 01:41:27,940
Oh, it's nowhere to be found!

1514
01:41:27,940 --> 01:41:29,020
What the hell, man?

1515
01:41:29,120 --> 01:41:30,040
How am I so lost?

1516
01:41:37,320 --> 01:41:37,680
Impossible.

1517
01:41:45,640 --> 01:41:46,480
Maybe over here.

1518
01:42:01,230 --> 01:42:01,990
There it is!

1519
01:42:03,650 --> 01:42:04,270
Spawn, baby!

1520
01:42:06,870 --> 01:42:08,070
Let's hope for some slimes.

1521
01:42:09,450 --> 01:42:10,630
I knew I was close.

1522
01:42:15,670 --> 01:42:16,750
How many beef am I at?

1523
01:42:16,870 --> 01:42:17,270
43!

1524
01:42:17,570 --> 01:42:17,770
Nice!

1525
01:42:19,690 --> 01:42:21,950
That's double the amount I got from my own farm.

1526
01:42:27,270 --> 01:42:27,670
Frogs.

1527
01:42:28,570 --> 01:42:30,070
Wait a minute, this is not spawn, actually.

1528
01:42:30,070 --> 01:42:32,270
Spawn is like a bit of a different biome.

1529
01:42:34,790 --> 01:42:36,130
Not sure what you would call it.

1530
01:42:36,230 --> 01:42:38,790
I guess I would call this one Louisiana or something.

1531
01:42:55,470 --> 01:42:56,930
Now where are the green guys?

1532
01:42:57,730 --> 01:42:58,830
Perhaps they come out at night.

1533
01:43:02,650 --> 01:43:04,150
Holy crap, there's a lot of animals though.

1534
01:43:22,770 --> 01:43:23,570
Are you stuck in the water?

1535
01:43:33,260 --> 01:43:33,940
There's nothing.

1536
01:43:36,840 --> 01:43:38,360
Don't tell me I came here for nothing.

1537
01:43:43,140 --> 01:43:44,500
I can't leave empty handed.

1538
01:43:49,480 --> 01:43:51,160
I mean, I got the meat, I guess, but...

1539
01:43:53,560 --> 01:43:54,820
Perhaps it is a night thing.

1540
01:43:55,200 --> 01:43:56,340
You gotta wait for night.

1541
01:44:02,780 --> 01:44:03,220
Uh...

1542
01:44:03,220 --> 01:44:04,340
Do you drop anything?

1543
01:44:05,180 --> 01:44:05,620
Okay.

1544
01:44:07,600 --> 01:44:09,760
I have yet to find anything from the frogs.

1545
01:44:21,990 --> 01:44:23,330
Yeah, they're definitely not here.

1546
01:44:35,300 --> 01:44:37,780
I also feel like I should be able to recognize some of this.

1547
01:44:40,910 --> 01:44:42,230
Did I just hear a...

1548
01:44:42,230 --> 01:44:42,990
Slime boy?

1549
01:44:47,920 --> 01:44:49,560
Oh, it's a frog!

1550
01:44:50,000 --> 01:44:50,440
Damn!

1551
01:44:52,200 --> 01:44:53,340
I got baited.

1552
01:44:57,880 --> 01:44:59,140
Okay, here's what we can try though.

1553
01:44:59,500 --> 01:45:01,820
So, I'm clearly in the swamp biome.

1554
01:45:03,360 --> 01:45:05,200
Let's try and dig down and see if we find a cave.

1555
01:45:05,340 --> 01:45:09,040
Because technically, if we find a cave, we should still be in the swamp biome.

1556
01:45:10,120 --> 01:45:12,300
And, uh, maybe down there, there's a lot of slimes.

1557
01:45:13,800 --> 01:45:14,660
That's my theory.

1558
01:45:17,780 --> 01:45:21,220
I just wanna find a good spot where we're definitely in the center of the biome, like over here.

1559
01:45:29,300 --> 01:45:30,180
I would say maybe...

1560
01:45:32,180 --> 01:45:35,860
Well, it's kinda like this is on the edge of something, so maybe over there is better.

1561
01:45:38,480 --> 01:45:41,900
I don't wanna accidentally wander off away from the biome down there.

1562
01:45:45,760 --> 01:45:48,320
I don't know why the color of the grass is changing like this.

1563
01:45:53,080 --> 01:45:55,460
But I mean, I guess, I guess this is, this would be it, right?

1564
01:45:57,040 --> 01:45:58,320
Let's just dig.

1565
01:45:58,560 --> 01:45:58,840
Fuck it.

1566
01:46:00,580 --> 01:46:01,920
We're not going straight down.

1567
01:46:02,200 --> 01:46:03,320
I learned that lesson.

1568
01:46:04,440 --> 01:46:05,360
Many times, in fact.

1569
01:46:09,170 --> 01:46:12,890
Oh, wait, I should've brought my, um, Silk Touch pickaxe.

1570
01:46:13,650 --> 01:46:17,550
Because it will produce more items from diamonds and stuff.

1571
01:46:18,250 --> 01:46:20,710
Now that we know how the crushing wheel works.

1572
01:46:28,980 --> 01:46:29,900
I hear a cave.

1573
01:46:33,580 --> 01:46:34,560
Nope, that's water.

1574
01:46:38,330 --> 01:46:39,250
That's also water.

1575
01:46:39,530 --> 01:46:39,710
Damn.

1576
01:46:41,210 --> 01:46:42,890
Maybe we make a little turn here.

1577
01:46:45,710 --> 01:46:46,630
That's also water.

1578
01:46:46,770 --> 01:46:47,170
Damn it!

1579
01:46:49,110 --> 01:46:50,710
Keep going, I believe.

1580
01:46:52,530 --> 01:46:54,090
Just keep blocking the water.

1581
01:47:00,080 --> 01:47:00,700
Circumvent it.

1582
01:47:03,400 --> 01:47:04,180
Here's a cave.

1583
01:47:07,940 --> 01:47:09,260
Oh, by the way!

1584
01:47:09,820 --> 01:47:12,460
There is one thing we have not found yet, by the way.

1585
01:47:12,640 --> 01:47:14,000
And that is...

1586
01:47:14,900 --> 01:47:15,380
Uh...

1587
01:47:15,940 --> 01:47:17,000
You know, the Shulker...

1588
01:47:17,640 --> 01:47:18,640
No, the Skulk!

1589
01:47:19,320 --> 01:47:20,180
Skulk areas!

1590
01:47:23,540 --> 01:47:25,260
We should really start looking for those.

1591
01:47:25,520 --> 01:47:27,440
Usually they're inside caves on the mountains.

1592
01:47:32,210 --> 01:47:36,050
Maybe some of the items in there will, um, unlock new things and create, you know?

1593
01:47:39,610 --> 01:47:41,090
I feel like this is a dead end down here.

1594
01:47:42,350 --> 01:47:44,050
But I'm gonna keep going a little longer.

1595
01:47:47,460 --> 01:47:48,220
More water.

1596
01:47:50,460 --> 01:47:51,460
Gosh dang it!

1597
01:47:53,280 --> 01:47:55,480
Nothing I hate more than water when I'm digging.

1598
01:47:56,920 --> 01:48:00,280
That has to be, like, one of the top bad things in Minecraft.

1599
01:48:07,110 --> 01:48:08,030
Uh, shovel...

1600
01:48:24,130 --> 01:48:25,610
Not even hearing any animals.

1601
01:48:41,520 --> 01:48:42,820
Okay, now we're getting deep.

1602
01:48:44,720 --> 01:48:45,120
And...

1603
01:48:47,260 --> 01:48:48,980
They're not gonna be down here, are they?

1604
01:48:50,640 --> 01:48:51,680
Let's try and go back up.

1605
01:48:51,780 --> 01:48:52,540
It's probably night now.

1606
01:48:52,680 --> 01:48:53,500
Maybe that will do something.

1607
01:48:53,620 --> 01:48:55,300
Maybe the slimy guys are here.

1608
01:48:58,840 --> 01:49:01,280
If they're not, then I honestly am at a loss.

1609
01:49:02,020 --> 01:49:03,560
No clue where to find them.

1610
01:49:05,060 --> 01:49:07,820
Or how to consistently get a hold of the green stuff.

1611
01:49:10,560 --> 01:49:11,220
It's night.

1612
01:49:23,250 --> 01:49:23,730
Anything?

1613
01:49:34,420 --> 01:49:35,160
Come on.

1614
01:49:41,860 --> 01:49:42,900
Look at this skeleton.

1615
01:49:43,960 --> 01:49:45,020
Filt with fungi.

1616
01:49:46,980 --> 01:49:48,220
I feel like that's a rare one.

1617
01:49:55,120 --> 01:49:56,260
Dude, there's nothing here.

1618
01:50:05,800 --> 01:50:06,780
That feels bad.

1619
01:50:12,330 --> 01:50:13,430
Did you see that jump?

1620
01:50:13,530 --> 01:50:14,530
That was a massive jump!

1621
01:50:16,670 --> 01:50:17,510
10 out of 10.

1622
01:50:27,380 --> 01:50:30,100
I mean, there's all kinds of monsters, just not the one I need.

1623
01:50:32,840 --> 01:50:39,260
My theory was that, okay, if they do indeed spawn in the caves in this biome, it's because it's dark down there, right?

1624
01:50:39,480 --> 01:50:42,260
And if it's night out here, maybe they also spawn on the surface.

1625
01:50:43,360 --> 01:50:44,120
Because it's night.

1626
01:50:46,920 --> 01:50:47,700
But there's nothing.

1627
01:50:51,510 --> 01:50:55,950
We're gonna have to go back to the drawing board on this and find a different way to get this green goop.

1628
01:51:00,870 --> 01:51:01,490
I'm out of here.

1629
01:51:11,440 --> 01:51:13,140
Being chased by a wolf, you love to see it.

1630
01:51:16,350 --> 01:51:19,670
And who knows, maybe on the way back we find the actual swamp that I was spawned in.

1631
01:51:25,320 --> 01:51:30,500
Like, I could have sworn I had seen green goop guys in the swamp, you know, at some point.

1632
01:51:37,850 --> 01:51:39,610
Kind of an interesting set of biomes here.

1633
01:51:49,960 --> 01:51:53,800
I think the next big thing we need to do is to go find Elytra.

1634
01:51:55,280 --> 01:51:57,300
That is, like, the huge thing right now.

1635
01:51:57,380 --> 01:52:00,760
Especially now that we have a way to get gunpowder very easily.

1636
01:52:01,540 --> 01:52:04,020
This will make things insanely efficient.

1637
01:52:07,290 --> 01:52:09,190
I also miss being able to fly around.

1638
01:52:16,540 --> 01:52:19,340
Wait, maybe if I collect stuff like this...

1639
01:52:20,560 --> 01:52:20,960
Like...

1640
01:52:22,420 --> 01:52:25,340
Maybe I can somehow make the green balls...

1641
01:52:26,420 --> 01:52:27,360
Okay, that doesn't work.

1642
01:52:27,440 --> 01:52:28,100
But maybe this stuff?

1643
01:52:29,460 --> 01:52:31,160
I think I need the gardening hose.

1644
01:52:35,280 --> 01:52:36,360
Don't have that right now.

1645
01:52:47,620 --> 01:52:48,700
Oh, it was a frog.

1646
01:52:50,620 --> 01:52:51,240
You know what?

1647
01:52:51,240 --> 01:52:51,800
I have a feeling.

1648
01:52:51,940 --> 01:52:53,220
Let me try one more dig.

1649
01:52:56,630 --> 01:52:57,350
Uno mas!

1650
01:52:59,490 --> 01:53:00,830
Let me also see here...

1651
01:53:00,830 --> 01:53:01,770
Yeah, yeah, actually, yes.

1652
01:53:04,090 --> 01:53:05,510
Let's try this one more time.

1653
01:53:06,810 --> 01:53:07,950
If we can find a cave.

1654
01:53:16,040 --> 01:53:16,680
Oh, damn.

1655
01:53:18,100 --> 01:53:19,060
Well, that's no good.

1656
01:53:19,640 --> 01:53:21,100
Let's try the other direction.

1657
01:53:22,900 --> 01:53:23,540
This way.

1658
01:53:29,120 --> 01:53:30,500
And then we can maybe turn right.

1659
01:53:32,060 --> 01:53:32,500
Here.

1660
01:53:44,740 --> 01:53:45,580
I hear something.

1661
01:53:53,140 --> 01:53:54,760
Isn't that the sound of a green guy?

1662
01:53:59,930 --> 01:54:00,650
Make a sound.

1663
01:54:04,710 --> 01:54:05,650
I went too deep?

1664
01:54:16,910 --> 01:54:17,650
Okay, whatever.

1665
01:54:19,810 --> 01:54:21,010
Maybe I'm imagining things.

1666
01:54:24,700 --> 01:54:26,020
Oh, I actually do need coal.

1667
01:54:39,230 --> 01:54:40,410
Get rid of...

1668
01:54:51,730 --> 01:54:54,070
Trust there's a cave down here, and there's gonna be green guys.

1669
01:54:58,220 --> 01:54:58,660
Ah!

1670
01:54:59,160 --> 01:55:00,260
Why you gotta do this to me?

1671
01:55:03,300 --> 01:55:04,240
I hate it.

1672
01:55:09,850 --> 01:55:10,290
Fine.

1673
01:55:10,510 --> 01:55:10,910
I'll leave.

1674
01:55:19,260 --> 01:55:20,740
In fact, now that I think about it.

1675
01:55:21,540 --> 01:55:24,260
Is the green guy the most rare creature in Minecraft?

1676
01:55:28,570 --> 01:55:30,870
Oh, it was the frog making that sound anyway.

1677
01:55:30,970 --> 01:55:31,750
It wasn't even the guy.

1678
